1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,003
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:44,043
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,879
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,429
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

7
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:06,692
[blade swooshing]

8
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,819
[♪ music swells]

9
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,033
[Gaeun panting]

10
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,452
[panting, breath trembling]

11
00:01:18,245 --> 00:01:20,079
- [stick taps twice]
- What are you doing?

12
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,832
[Gaeun, breath trembling]

13
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:24,834
Gaeun, what's wrong?

14
00:01:24,835 --> 00:01:26,794
[breathing heavily]

15
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:28,589
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

16
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:32,509
I'm the lead dancer.

17
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,305
I'm the lead dancer.

18
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:40,601
- [barks]
- [K9 handler] Shush. [mutters]

19
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,399
SONG GAEUN

20
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:52,028
I'm the lead dancer. [gasping shakily]

21
00:01:52,029 --> 00:01:53,196
[Dahye] Hey...

22
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:56,199
[♪ music swells]

23
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,622
- [sharp swoosh, slash]
- [shrieks, echoing]

24
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:04,624
[♪ music fades]

25
00:02:05,334 --> 00:02:07,294
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

26
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:11,673
[Gaeun gasping shakily]

27
00:02:13,175 --> 00:02:15,260
[breathing heavily]

28
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:22,516
[♪ music increases in tempo]

29
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,061
[panting, gasping]

30
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:32,444
[sword clatters]

31
00:02:33,612 --> 00:02:34,945
[gasping]

32
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:37,032
[panting, gasping]

33
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:41,703
[♪ music swells]

34
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:46,166
[Gaeun continues panting]

35
00:02:47,918 --> 00:02:49,169
[♪ music fades]

36
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:51,837
[siren blaring]

37
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:53,423
[students whispering anxiously]

38
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:01,473
EPISODE 10

39
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:04,810
Is the culprit among them?

40
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:07,062
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

41
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:12,191
How did it go?

42
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:14,026
We found some traces here and there.

43
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:16,153
But we can't narrow down a suspect.

44
00:03:16,154 --> 00:03:18,240
Too many people use this space.

45
00:03:19,408 --> 00:03:20,992
- Okay. Thank you for coming.
- [K9 handler] Sure.

46
00:03:25,414 --> 00:03:26,540
What happened?

47
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:30,167
A curse pouch was found in Seyeon's bag,

48
00:03:30,168 --> 00:03:31,211
and it had drugs inside.

49
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,003
Drugs?

50
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:35,340
Gaeun was hallucinating
because of the same drug.

51
00:03:40,137 --> 00:03:43,432
Are you saying one of my students
did something like that?

52
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:47,936
Don't tell the students anything just yet.

53
00:03:57,446 --> 00:03:58,654
[♪ music fades]

54
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:01,031
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

55
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:03,075
[Junyoung] This is
commonly known as "Ruby."

56
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:05,453
Just touching it can make you hallucinate.

57
00:04:05,454 --> 00:04:08,831
It's sold anonymously on the dark web,
so they can't identify the buyers.

58
00:04:08,832 --> 00:04:10,207
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

59
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:11,459
CONTACT WITH NARCOTIC SUBSTANCE

60
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:13,002
HALLUCINATION
REPEATEDLY STRUCK LEGS

61
00:04:13,003 --> 00:04:16,964
So Seyeon touched those rubies
and died from an asthma attack?

62
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:18,299
Yes.

63
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,801
They may not have intended it,
but it ended in a murder.

64
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,553
But even so,

65
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:25,639
could a high school student get
their hands on a drug like this?

66
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,310
It's not impossible.
The dark web doesn't have an age limit.

67
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,269
[Isoo] I don't understand

68
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,396
cursing someone
just to steal the lead role.

69
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:34,566
I heard the arts festival
is a pretty big deal.

70
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:37,235
All the famous
dance companies will be there.

71
00:04:37,861 --> 00:04:39,654
We can't trace the drug,

72
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,364
so we'll have to go after the curse pouch.

73
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:44,116
Check the footage from the Witch's Shop.

74
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:46,410
Make a list of everyone
who bought a curse pouch.

75
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,787
Got it.

76
00:04:47,788 --> 00:04:49,623
[♪ music increases in tempo]

77
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:57,798
[keyboard clacks]

78
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,008
Detective Joo.

79
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:02,719
A student bought one
the day before the incident.

80
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:08,433
[♪ music swells]

81
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:12,770
[♪ music resumes tempo]

82
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:13,939
That's Hayun.

83
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:19,194
[♪ music fades]

84
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,407
Hi, Hayun.

85
00:05:27,619 --> 00:05:29,287
Can we talk for a moment?

86
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,414
[Isoo] Hayun, what will you have?

87
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:33,874
I'm fine.

88
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,836
You should eat something.

89
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,672
Then I'll get the Chicken Bacon Mini Wrap.

90
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:42,341
Okay. Italian B.M.T. for you,
Detective Joo?

91
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:43,676
Yeah. Coffee, too.

92
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:45,303
Coffee? What about you, Hayun?

93
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:47,429
I'll just drink water.

94
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,641
No. Jin Isoo is buying today.

95
00:05:50,559 --> 00:05:51,810
Want anything more to eat, huh?

96
00:05:53,937 --> 00:05:56,313
You must be startled
after what happened with Gaeun.

97
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:58,400
Yeah, why did she do that?

98
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,901
I'm not sure.

99
00:06:01,236 --> 00:06:03,697
Have your friends said anything about it?

100
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:07,241
They said maybe she lost it
after getting the lead.

101
00:06:07,242 --> 00:06:08,451
Ah. [chuckles softly]

102
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:13,999
[Isoo] Mmm.

103
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,251
[♪ jaunty, dramatic music playing]

104
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:19,212
All right.

105
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:22,923
Here, drink this.

106
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,342
Coffee for Detective Joo.

107
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:25,886
Let's eat.

108
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:27,637
[softly] Mmm...

109
00:06:30,015 --> 00:06:31,099
Mmm!

110
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,145
Mmm!

111
00:06:36,146 --> 00:06:37,229
It's good, right?

112
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,772
- Right?
- Yes.

113
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,733
You girls are always on a diet, huh.

114
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:42,402
You need to eat well for your arm to heal.

115
00:06:47,616 --> 00:06:49,242
Can you pick that up for me?

116
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:53,580
[♪ music fades]

117
00:06:58,043 --> 00:06:59,044
You're right.

118
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:01,880
I put this inside Seyeon's bag.

119
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,007
Gaeun, too?

120
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:08,261
Gaeun? What about Gaeun?

121
00:07:11,306 --> 00:07:12,724
But how did you know?

122
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,559
Mmm.

123
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:16,186
The security camera.

124
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,314
[chuckles nervously, swears softly]

125
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:21,608
So, what about it?

126
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,527
[wrapper crumpling]

127
00:07:25,487 --> 00:07:27,530
Seyeon died because of that pouch.

128
00:07:30,367 --> 00:07:32,077
Is this a real curse?

129
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:34,787
I was only messing around.

130
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:35,789
No.

131
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:39,291
There was a drug inside
that causes hallucinations.

132
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,376
What?

133
00:07:40,377 --> 00:07:41,543
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

134
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:42,921
What are you talking about?

135
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:45,215
Uh, if, by any chance,

136
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,216
you put it in as a joke--

137
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:49,386
What are you talking about?
Do you think I'm crazy?

138
00:07:52,347 --> 00:07:54,098
It really wasn't me.

139
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:56,685
I did it because I was annoyed.
Where would I even get drugs?

140
00:07:58,144 --> 00:07:59,813
If I got caught, I'd be expelled.

141
00:08:00,939 --> 00:08:02,773
And everyone at school does this.

142
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:04,733
They send curses
to people they don't like.

143
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:06,235
The principal knows as well.

144
00:08:06,236 --> 00:08:07,779
Some kids had theirs confiscated.

145
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:09,655
The principal knows, too?

146
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:11,324
Yes. Go ask her.

147
00:08:12,951 --> 00:08:14,536
When did you put the pouch in?

148
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:21,834
During the afternoon class
on the day Seyeon died.

149
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:23,837
CHANGING ROOM

150
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:30,844
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

151
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,071
MOON SEYEON

152
00:08:57,746 --> 00:09:00,081
I got really scared
when she actually died.

153
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:05,294
[♪ music fades]

154
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:07,838
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

155
00:09:07,839 --> 00:09:08,922
KIM HAYUN

156
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:11,342
I don't think Hayun is the culprit.

157
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:13,385
Detective Choi.

158
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:15,971
Let's see the hallway
outside the studio that afternoon.

159
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:17,056
Okay.

160
00:09:17,057 --> 00:09:18,892
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

161
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:41,873
Did Hayun just put the pouch in?

162
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:09,400
- Wait.
- [keyboard clacks]

163
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,360
What's this?

164
00:10:11,361 --> 00:10:12,987
[Junyoung] Principal Jeong Joohee?

165
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,533
The principal slipped in the drugs?

166
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,868
The principal killed Seyeon?

167
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:21,830
She has no reason to.

168
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,707
She said she gave Seyeon
the lead because of her asthma.

169
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,292
She might've gone in to get something.

170
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:30,338
Anyone could have gotten to Seyeon's bag.

171
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,841
If all those students
are giving each other curses,

172
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:35,593
how can we narrow down the suspects?

173
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:38,096
[sighs softly]

174
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,850
Did you find anything on Seyeon's phone?

175
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:44,519
Nothing significant.

176
00:10:47,522 --> 00:10:48,689
[sighs softly]

177
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:50,357
I CURSE YOU, MOON SEYEON
DIE, DIE!

178
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:51,609
By the way,

179
00:10:52,402 --> 00:10:54,945
if she wanted to curse someone,
why not write their name?

180
00:10:54,946 --> 00:10:56,947
Why just write that she cursed them?

181
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:59,658
Maybe she wanted to curse multiple people.

182
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,743
Like the ones responsible for her death.

183
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:04,705
But there wasn't anyone like that.

184
00:11:04,706 --> 00:11:06,166
[♪ music swells]

185
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,004
[♪ music fades]

186
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,006
Huh?

187
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,508
[♪ suspenseful music plays, swells]

188
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:18,594
I CURSE YOU

189
00:11:18,595 --> 00:11:20,137
[in English] What the...
[in Korean] Oh, my God!

190
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:21,555
[♪ music fades]

191
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:23,473
Hey, come here.

192
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:26,101
- What is it?
- I think I'm a freaking genius.

193
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,436
Look.

194
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:29,480
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

195
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,779
JEONG JOOHEE

196
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,865
[gasps]

197
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:42,368
"Jeong Joohee"?

198
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:49,125
Maybe what Yuna actually wanted
to write was "Jeong Joohee."

199
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:54,130
Jeong Joohee was the one
who killed Baek Yuna?

200
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,800
She made her kill herself?

201
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,636
But why?

202
00:12:00,303 --> 00:12:02,597
She even received money
from Baek Yuna's parents.

203
00:12:03,598 --> 00:12:05,975
Jeong Joohee is suspicious, though.

204
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:10,521
Right. She knew about the curse pouch,
but pretended not to.

205
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:15,526
What's this?

206
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,320
Have you never seen it before?

207
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:20,572
It's a trend among the students.

208
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:21,950
It's a curse pouch.

209
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:24,869
The students carry this around?

210
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:29,998
Gaeun also said something, too.

211
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:31,584
But Seyeon told me

212
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:35,088
the principal has no choice
but to pick her for the lead.

213
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:41,678
Seyeon didn't have the money to bribe her,

214
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:46,765
so why did Jeong Joohee have
no choice but to pick her as the lead?

215
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:48,101
[♪ music swells]

216
00:12:54,399 --> 00:12:57,526
JEONG JOOHEE

217
00:12:57,527 --> 00:12:58,569
[♪ music fades]

218
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:01,238
[Isoo] Ma'am,

219
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:04,909
it seems the principal
was very fond of Seyeon.

220
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:07,286
She was.

221
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:08,996
She came to see me.

222
00:13:08,997 --> 00:13:11,832
Principal Jeong Joohee came to see you?

223
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:12,875
[Grandma] Yes.

224
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,626
She said she felt bad.

225
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:16,003
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

226
00:13:16,004 --> 00:13:17,755
She brought that with her.

227
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:23,720
Thank you for coming all the way
to this humble place, Principal Jeong.

228
00:13:24,721 --> 00:13:26,597
You must be heartbroken.

229
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:32,894
<i>But she said
she had left something with Seyeon.</i>

230
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,731
[drawer opens, rummaging]

231
00:13:36,149 --> 00:13:37,232
[drawer closes]

232
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,317
[drawer opens]

233
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:39,861
[♪ music increases in tempo]

234
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:41,945
[rummaging continues]

235
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,239
She searched Seyeon's room?

236
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,323
[Grandma] Yes.

237
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:48,493
But I don't think she found it.

238
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:49,953
She just left.

239
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:51,289
[♪ music resumes tempo]

240
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:54,207
And you have no idea what it was?

241
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:56,127
No, I wouldn't know.

242
00:13:57,879 --> 00:13:59,004
[♪ music fades]

243
00:13:59,005 --> 00:14:00,048
Ma'am.

244
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:03,426
[exhales softly]
I figured you wouldn't have eaten.

245
00:14:04,886 --> 00:14:05,969
[♪ melancholy music playing]

246
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:08,181
I don't know
if it's worth living like this.

247
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:11,392
I outlived my daughter,

248
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:15,271
and now I even lost

249
00:14:16,022 --> 00:14:17,899
my poor granddaughter. [sobbing]

250
00:14:25,198 --> 00:14:26,406
[♪ music fades]

251
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,657
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

252
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:29,660
[shaman] <i>An item with fur, about this big.</i>

253
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:31,995
<i>She left it behind.</i>

254
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:33,164
Ma'am.

255
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,543
Is this your phone?

256
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:39,795
What's the matter?

257
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:41,589
The shaman said she saw this.

258
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:45,134
It used to be Seyeon's phone.

259
00:14:46,094 --> 00:14:48,221
She gave it to me a few months ago.

260
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,264
May I take a look?

261
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,891
Of course.

262
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,101
- Feel free to.
- Okay.

263
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:55,478
[♪ music increases in tempo]

264
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:02,485
This is a video app.

265
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:05,904
Ma'am, do you know what this is?

266
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,864
I don't know any of that stuff.

267
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,242
Ah. I'm going to take a look.

268
00:15:10,243 --> 00:15:11,660
- [Grandma] Okay.
- Thanks.

269
00:15:11,661 --> 00:15:13,121
- [♪ music swells]
- [Isoo inhales sharply]

270
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,749
ALL VIDEOS

271
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,627
[♪ music slows, turns ominous]

272
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:28,010
[♪ music swells]

273
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:31,973
[♪ music resumes tempo]

274
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:33,891
[phone case snaps shut]

275
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:37,520
Ma'am.

276
00:15:38,813 --> 00:15:40,605
Make sure you eat properly.

277
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:42,649
Please stay healthy.

278
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:46,070
We promise to catch the culprit
who did this to Seyeon.

279
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:48,406
Thank you.

280
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:54,370
[♪ music fades]

281
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:01,586
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

282
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,715
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

283
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:08,091
[indistinct chatter]

284
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:09,886
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

285
00:16:43,044 --> 00:16:44,212
[spectral exhale]

286
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,338
[spectral exhale]

287
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:47,423
[♪ music swells]

288
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:50,258
[♪ music fades]

289
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,344
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

290
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:53,638
[indistinct chatter]

291
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:58,309
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

292
00:17:01,479 --> 00:17:03,313
[Isoo] No more cursing each other.

293
00:17:03,314 --> 00:17:06,816
You should all be
sharing good luck instead, okay?

294
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:08,444
- [students] Okay.
- [Isoo] Here.

295
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:10,029
[in English] Good luck.

296
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:11,614
[in Korean] Here you go.

297
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,991
Here you go.

298
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:17,328
We came to see the performance, too.

299
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:18,870
Sure.

300
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,205
I hope you enjoy the show.

301
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:22,333
Yes, I'm sure it'll be very enjoyable.

302
00:17:24,502 --> 00:17:25,877
All right, you got this!

303
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:27,171
- We got this!
- We got this!

304
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:30,173
Everyone ready?

305
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:31,341
- Yes.
- Yes.

306
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:33,261
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

307
00:17:36,222 --> 00:17:37,305
[door closes]

308
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:38,599
[AV technician] Who are you?

309
00:17:39,934 --> 00:17:40,977
Excuse me for a moment.

310
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:42,937
Ah, right.

311
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,398
[♪ music fades]

312
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,986
[footsteps approaching, heels clicking]

313
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:55,490
Thank you all for joining us at
the Juyeon Arts High School Arts Festival.

314
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,075
Juyeon Arts High School

315
00:17:57,076 --> 00:18:01,413
has grown into a prestigious school
known for producing exceptional dancers,

316
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:04,583
and we owe much of that success
to one special person.

317
00:18:04,584 --> 00:18:08,169
I'd like to introduce you all
to Principal Jeong Joohee,

318
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:10,922
who leads our school
with nothing but love for her students.

319
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,300
[all applauding, cheering]

320
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:20,141
Whoo!

321
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:28,190
[all applauding, cheering loudly]

322
00:18:31,152 --> 00:18:32,569
[applauding, cheering fades]

323
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:36,616
I'd like to thank our distinguished guests
for taking the time to join us today.

324
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:40,953
Recently, a tragic event
befell our school.

325
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:46,459
Despite their grief, our students
worked hard to prepare this performance.

326
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:49,294
I would be grateful

327
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:51,881
if you could give them
your warmest support.

328
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:54,258
[all applauding]

329
00:18:58,346 --> 00:18:59,597
[applauding fades]

330
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,227
WHEN A NAME BECOMES A GENRE OF ITS OWN

331
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,938
[♪ upbeat, dramatic music playing]

332
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:14,654
JEONG JOOHEE, THE DANCER
WHO HAS DEFINED AN ERA OF KOREAN DANCE

333
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:21,243
HER NAME IS NOW A DIRECTION

334
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:26,123
THE REASON KOREAN DANCE
KEPT MOVING FORWARD

335
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:29,501
NOW SHE FOCUSES ON NURTURING TALENT

336
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:30,878
[all applauding]

337
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:34,047
AN EDUCATOR OF BOTH DANCE AND CHARACTER

338
00:19:34,048 --> 00:19:36,132
AN ICON SETTING THE STANDARD
FOR THE NEXT GENERATION

339
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:40,262
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
WILL CARRY ON HER LEGACY

340
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:42,305
- [video, music stop abruptly]
- [projector clicks]

341
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:43,765
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

342
00:19:43,766 --> 00:19:45,058
[utility knife clicking]

343
00:19:45,059 --> 00:19:46,811
- [slices]
- [all gasp]

344
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,855
[all murmuring anxiously]

345
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:56,570
[anxious murmuring intensifies]

346
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,785
Mr. Park, what's going on?
Turn that off right now!

347
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:04,869
- [radio clicks off]
- [audience exclaiming]

348
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,330
It's okay.

349
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:10,875
[audience gasping, exclaiming]

350
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,169
[mic thuds, whines]

351
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:16,590
[students scream]

352
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:19,342
[panting] Girls.

353
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:20,927
This isn't real.

354
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:22,471
It's all fake.

355
00:20:32,273 --> 00:20:33,983
[audience murmuring anxiously]

356
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:39,196
[panting frantically]

357
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,037
[Juhee sighs, whimpers]

358
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,498
[audience continues murmuring]

359
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:53,835
[breath trembles] No.

360
00:20:53,836 --> 00:20:55,712
It's all a lie.

361
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:57,088
You're a murderer.

362
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,215
It's on video.
What do you mean it's a lie?

363
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:01,468
[audience members jeering]

364
00:21:01,469 --> 00:21:03,763
[gasping sharply, yelling]
I said, it's not true!

365
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:05,431
[♪ ominous music playing]

366
00:21:07,016 --> 00:21:08,100
[spectral exhale]

367
00:21:09,185 --> 00:21:10,311
[softly] Girls.

368
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:13,605
[whimpering shakily]

369
00:21:13,606 --> 00:21:15,064
[gasping sharply]

370
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,567
[whimpering shakily]

371
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:21,739
[audience murmuring anxiously]

372
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,371
[♪ music swells]

373
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:35,211
[whimpering shakily, gasps]

374
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:37,670
[thuds]

375
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:39,131
[audience exclaiming]

376
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:45,011
[spectator] Shouldn't we
call an ambulance?

377
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:46,679
[all murmuring anxiously]

378
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,557
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

379
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:56,899
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

380
00:22:05,908 --> 00:22:07,201
Why did you kill her?

381
00:22:09,662 --> 00:22:10,830
Baek Yuna.

382
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:17,127
She didn't know her place.

383
00:22:21,090 --> 00:22:22,257
[♪ music fades]

384
00:22:22,258 --> 00:22:23,466
[Yuna] <i>Ms. Jeong.</i>

385
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:24,676
7 MONTHS AGO

386
00:22:24,677 --> 00:22:25,844
Am I not talented?

387
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:26,928
[scoffs]

388
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:28,304
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

389
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:29,931
What are you talking about?

390
00:22:29,932 --> 00:22:32,475
You're exceptionally gifted.

391
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:34,812
Then why did you take money from my mom?

392
00:22:36,397 --> 00:22:38,482
Did I get the lead because of the money?

393
00:22:39,275 --> 00:22:41,985
You even told her
you'd get me into college no matter what.

394
00:22:41,986 --> 00:22:44,154
That's not playing fair.

395
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,073
[scoffs softly]

396
00:22:48,242 --> 00:22:49,410
Yuna.

397
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:53,330
Having money

398
00:22:55,416 --> 00:22:56,876
is a talent.

399
00:22:58,043 --> 00:23:00,295
You're probably too young to understand.

400
00:23:00,296 --> 00:23:01,589
Playing fair?

401
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:04,008
That's all an illusion.

402
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,635
Nothing is fair in this world.

403
00:23:07,261 --> 00:23:09,178
Everything's decided
the moment you're born.

404
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:10,472
Just like your genes.

405
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:14,226
You can't last in this industry
without money anyway.

406
00:23:14,894 --> 00:23:17,478
So stop being so childish,

407
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:20,274
and just enjoy the benefits
of having wealthy parents, huh?

408
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:23,611
I don't want to.

409
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:26,780
What?

410
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:30,116
I want to be recognized for my own talent.

411
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:31,160
[scoffs softly]

412
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:34,204
What are you going to do about it?

413
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:35,998
Turn yourself in.

414
00:23:36,916 --> 00:23:38,876
Otherwise, I'm going to report you myself.

415
00:23:44,632 --> 00:23:45,925
[♪ music swells]

416
00:23:47,009 --> 00:23:48,052
[door opens]

417
00:23:48,886 --> 00:23:49,929
[door closes]

418
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:52,306
[♪ music fades]

419
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:56,352
[cell phone vibrating]

420
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:00,689
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

421
00:24:03,734 --> 00:24:05,234
Yes, Ms. Ryu.

422
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:08,238
<i>Hello, Principal Jeong.
Have you been well?</i>

423
00:24:08,781 --> 00:24:09,948
Yes.

424
00:24:09,949 --> 00:24:13,910
<i>I have the bag you mentioned last time.</i>

425
00:24:13,911 --> 00:24:15,412
<i>I'll stop by to see you soon.</i>

426
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:17,122
Ah.

427
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:18,916
Yes, all right.

428
00:24:22,044 --> 00:24:23,169
[line disconnects]

429
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:25,297
[♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

430
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:34,138
You came to practice. [chuckles]

431
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:35,474
You changed your mind, right?

432
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:38,351
You made the right choice.

433
00:24:38,352 --> 00:24:40,980
Acting all righteous
won't do you any good.

434
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:54,826
[♪ music fades]

435
00:24:54,827 --> 00:24:56,578
I came to practice one last time.

436
00:24:57,246 --> 00:24:58,329
One last time?

437
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,249
Turn yourself in by tomorrow.

438
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:02,875
I'm going to quit everything, too.

439
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:04,795
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

440
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:36,452
[seat belt unbuckles]

441
00:25:54,011 --> 00:25:55,137
[spectral exhale]

442
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:58,974
[♪ ominous music playing]

443
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:05,813
[clicking]

444
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:07,274
[♪ ominous sting]

445
00:26:08,317 --> 00:26:09,860
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

446
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:23,581
[spectral exhale]

447
00:26:23,582 --> 00:26:25,417
[♪ woman vocalizing gently]

448
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:36,094
[♪ vocalizing, music fades]

449
00:26:36,095 --> 00:26:37,930
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

450
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:46,897
[sniffling, crying]

451
00:26:54,822 --> 00:26:56,448
[sniffles, breath trembles]

452
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:02,037
Yuna.

453
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:05,998
I know how you feel. [inhales shakily]

454
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:07,751
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

455
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:12,047
[exhales softly]
It's all been so hard on you.

456
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:14,882
You haven't been able to sleep,

457
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:17,802
and I heard
you're even taking antidepressants.

458
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:19,304
[voice shaking] Ms. Jeong.

459
00:27:23,016 --> 00:27:25,309
You love dancing.

460
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:28,146
How could you give it up, right?

461
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:40,450
I'm taking antidepressants because of you.

462
00:27:41,159 --> 00:27:42,953
I've known for a while

463
00:27:43,787 --> 00:27:45,122
that my mom gave you money.

464
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:49,083
I thought about looking the other way,

465
00:27:49,084 --> 00:27:52,254
because my mom and I would
also be blamed if this got out.

466
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:55,757
[breathes shakily] Yuna.

467
00:27:57,634 --> 00:27:59,719
This won't be for long.

468
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:01,305
If you just get through this,

469
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:05,391
you'll become the best dancer there is.

470
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:06,893
[♪ tense, melancholy music playing]

471
00:28:06,894 --> 00:28:08,312
[Juhee's breath trembling]

472
00:28:16,153 --> 00:28:18,196
I don't want to end up like you.

473
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:23,492
What?

474
00:28:23,493 --> 00:28:24,828
Ms. Jeong.

475
00:28:25,621 --> 00:28:28,206
dance was the one thing I loved most,
and you corrupted it.

476
00:28:37,174 --> 00:28:38,425
Take back what you just said.

477
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,471
If you say you're sorry,

478
00:28:44,473 --> 00:28:45,974
I'll forgive you just this once.

479
00:28:47,351 --> 00:28:48,393
I'm...

480
00:28:49,478 --> 00:28:50,854
giving you a chance.

481
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:52,813
No.

482
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,483
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

483
00:28:55,776 --> 00:28:57,026
Let go.

484
00:28:57,027 --> 00:28:58,403
[utility knife clicking]

485
00:28:58,987 --> 00:29:00,071
[Juhee grunts]

486
00:29:00,072 --> 00:29:02,156
[gasps incredulously, breathing heavily]

487
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:03,241
[utility knife clatters]

488
00:29:03,867 --> 00:29:05,077
[breath trembling] Ms. Jeong.

489
00:29:05,661 --> 00:29:07,037
[Juhee] Don't resent me.

490
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:10,998
You made me do this.

491
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:12,292
[♪ music swells]

492
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,339
[♪ music resumes tempo]

493
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:20,550
[breathing raggedly]

494
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:39,151
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

495
00:29:39,152 --> 00:29:40,487
[grunts, gasps]

496
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:43,240
[continues breathing raggedly]

497
00:29:47,869 --> 00:29:49,621
[♪ music increases in tempo]

498
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:54,042
[gasping sharply]

499
00:30:02,426 --> 00:30:03,635
[groans softly]

500
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:14,061
[whimpers weakly]

501
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:15,772
[♪ music swells]

502
00:30:25,115 --> 00:30:26,533
[♪ music resumes tempo]

503
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:32,121
She's like this until the end.
[clicks tongue]

504
00:30:32,122 --> 00:30:34,373
JEONG JOOHEE

505
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:35,834
[♪ music increases in tempo]

506
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:15,831
I CURSE YOU

507
00:31:15,832 --> 00:31:19,044
- [♪ music resumes tempo]
- [Yuna] <i>Mom, I'm sorry.</i>

508
00:31:25,050 --> 00:31:26,176
[♪ music fades]

509
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:27,928
[crying softly]

510
00:31:30,639 --> 00:31:32,224
It was killing me, too.

511
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:37,604
Yuna haunted my dreams every night,
and I couldn't sleep.

512
00:31:39,064 --> 00:31:40,774
No medication would work,

513
00:31:42,901 --> 00:31:44,860
and I even turned to drugs because of her.

514
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:46,655
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

515
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:49,199
But then,

516
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:56,331
there was another student
who didn't know her place.

517
00:32:06,258 --> 00:32:07,342
[glass clinks]

518
00:32:09,136 --> 00:32:10,302
[exhales sharply]

519
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:11,471
[breathing deeply]

520
00:32:17,853 --> 00:32:19,979
- [knock at door]
- [gasps softly]

521
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:21,148
[door opens]

522
00:32:22,315 --> 00:32:23,567
[♪ music fades]

523
00:32:24,234 --> 00:32:25,735
- Oh.
- [door closes]

524
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:29,030
It's you, Seyeon. What can I do for you?

525
00:32:29,656 --> 00:32:32,826
I have something to tell you.

526
00:32:34,119 --> 00:32:36,580
I'm a bit busy right now.
Let's talk another time.

527
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:42,210
This won't take long.

528
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:45,255
What is it? Make it quick.

529
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:50,260
I wish I could give you
a lot of money as well,

530
00:32:51,511 --> 00:32:53,513
but my family isn't well-off.

531
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:57,517
I can't even afford private lessons.

532
00:33:00,562 --> 00:33:05,358
So I was secretly recording
your tutoring sessions with Yuna.

533
00:33:07,027 --> 00:33:08,528
[♪ ominous music playing]

534
00:33:31,301 --> 00:33:33,428
- [utility knife slices]
- [Yuna gasps incredulously]

535
00:33:34,638 --> 00:33:36,014
[utility knife clatters over recording]

536
00:33:36,389 --> 00:33:38,182
[Yuna, breath trembling]

537
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:39,935
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

538
00:33:44,064 --> 00:33:45,774
[sighs softly] You know,

539
00:33:46,942 --> 00:33:49,277
I'd actually given up on everything.

540
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:54,323
Only five students can go to
Hankuk University from our department.

541
00:33:54,324 --> 00:33:57,160
And they'll all be students
from rich, powerful families.

542
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:02,249
Whereas I have nothing.

543
00:34:05,085 --> 00:34:07,337
But then this opportunity came along.

544
00:34:10,131 --> 00:34:11,466
[chuckles nervously]

545
00:34:13,301 --> 00:34:14,678
[stuttering] Seyeon.

546
00:34:16,680 --> 00:34:18,807
Does anyone else know about this?

547
00:34:19,808 --> 00:34:22,977
[chuckles] Of course not.
No one else can know.

548
00:34:22,978 --> 00:34:25,062
I can't have you getting arrested.

549
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:26,314
Seyeon,

550
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:29,400
you can't do this. Delete that right now.

551
00:34:29,401 --> 00:34:31,319
Can a teacher kill her student?

552
00:34:33,738 --> 00:34:37,284
All you have to do
is favor me from now on.

553
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:43,248
Start by making me
the lead dancer in the festival.

554
00:34:46,293 --> 00:34:48,920
Don't even think about trying anything.

555
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:53,883
I'm not like Yuna.
I won't be easy to deal with.

556
00:34:58,054 --> 00:34:59,306
[♪ music increases in tempo]

557
00:35:00,140 --> 00:35:01,224
[scoffs]

558
00:35:02,267 --> 00:35:04,727
I'll keep this nice and safe
so no one finds out.

559
00:35:04,728 --> 00:35:05,854
Don't worry about that.

560
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:09,691
I'll delete it
once I get into Hankuk University.

561
00:35:11,234 --> 00:35:12,569
[♪ music swells]

562
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:17,949
[door opens, closes]

563
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:19,825
[♪ music fades]

564
00:35:19,826 --> 00:35:22,579
So I did exactly as Seyeon asked,

565
00:35:25,332 --> 00:35:29,336
but the parents of the student originally
chosen for the lead kept calling me.

566
00:35:30,587 --> 00:35:34,466
They kept hounding me
about how much Seyeon had paid me.

567
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:38,511
You even killed someone
after taking a bribe,

568
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:41,014
yet you accepted money again?

569
00:35:42,182 --> 00:35:44,099
You think I asked for it?

570
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:46,019
They come to me on their own.

571
00:35:46,728 --> 00:35:50,397
They come with designer bags and cash,
asking me to look after their kid.

572
00:35:50,398 --> 00:35:52,941
Is that why you decided
to kill Seyeon as well?

573
00:35:52,942 --> 00:35:54,819
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

574
00:35:55,654 --> 00:35:56,655
[inhales sharply]

575
00:35:58,657 --> 00:36:01,993
That wasn't my intention from the start.

576
00:36:02,744 --> 00:36:03,828
I was...

577
00:36:05,330 --> 00:36:07,123
just wondering what I should do,

578
00:36:07,916 --> 00:36:09,000
then...

579
00:36:10,502 --> 00:36:12,878
I went online to get some drugs.

580
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:14,798
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

581
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:16,424
[exhales softly]

582
00:36:21,930 --> 00:36:25,015
GOT SOMETHING NEW, WANNA TRY?

583
00:36:25,016 --> 00:36:27,267
WHAT IS IT?

584
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:29,144
SOMETHING THAT FEELS GOOD
JUST BY TOUCHING IT

585
00:36:29,145 --> 00:36:30,522
BUT BAD FOR HEART CONDITION OR ASTHMA

586
00:36:31,106 --> 00:36:33,399
[keyboard clacking]

587
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:36,736
WHY? WHAT HAPPENS?

588
00:36:37,404 --> 00:36:40,239
WORST CASE, YOU DIE

589
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:42,951
[♪ ominous sting]

590
00:36:44,452 --> 00:36:45,787
[♪ music resumes tempo]

591
00:36:47,664 --> 00:36:48,748
[door opens]

592
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:53,293
- [student 1] Hello.
- [student 2] Hello.

593
00:36:53,294 --> 00:36:54,379
Warm up.

594
00:36:58,425 --> 00:36:59,467
[sighs softly]

595
00:37:00,927 --> 00:37:02,220
[♪ music turns ominous]

596
00:37:12,147 --> 00:37:14,648
- [switch clicks]
- Warm up and start rehearsing.

597
00:37:14,649 --> 00:37:15,775
- Yes, ma'am.
- [students] Yes, ma'am.

598
00:37:17,777 --> 00:37:18,903
MOON SEYEON

599
00:37:25,118 --> 00:37:26,745
[♪ music increases in tempo]

600
00:37:35,420 --> 00:37:37,255
[♪ ominous, ticking music playing]

601
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:47,474
[♪ music swells]

602
00:37:53,438 --> 00:37:54,855
[♪ music resumes tempo]

603
00:37:54,856 --> 00:37:56,608
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

604
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:09,204
[spectral whoosh]

605
00:38:09,829 --> 00:38:11,122
[spectral exhale]

606
00:38:12,582 --> 00:38:14,375
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

607
00:38:15,210 --> 00:38:16,377
[blade swooshing]

608
00:38:19,005 --> 00:38:20,548
- [♪ music stops]
- [panting]

609
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,384
[♪ music turns ominous]

610
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:30,265
[Yuna] Seyeon.

611
00:38:30,266 --> 00:38:32,559
Please... help me.

612
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:34,062
- [spectral exhale]
- [sword clatters]

613
00:38:35,605 --> 00:38:37,523
Don't come any closer.

614
00:38:37,524 --> 00:38:38,690
Stay away from me!

615
00:38:38,691 --> 00:38:41,777
Seyeon, please help me.

616
00:38:41,778 --> 00:38:43,195
[screaming]

617
00:38:43,196 --> 00:38:44,571
[blunt thudding]

618
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:46,282
[continues screaming]

619
00:38:50,370 --> 00:38:51,788
[gasping frantically, grunting]

620
00:38:53,248 --> 00:38:55,415
[♪ music swells, fades]

621
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:57,252
- [wheezing heavily]
- [sword clatters]

622
00:38:57,919 --> 00:38:59,837
[♪ soft, somber music playing]

623
00:38:59,838 --> 00:39:01,089
[wheezing, choking]

624
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:10,223
[Isoo] You're the one who slipped
Gaeun the drugs as well, right?

625
00:39:11,933 --> 00:39:14,977
To make it look like
an incident between the students.

626
00:39:14,978 --> 00:39:16,980
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

627
00:39:18,857 --> 00:39:19,858
SONG GAEUN

628
00:39:26,072 --> 00:39:27,115
[scoffs]

629
00:39:27,699 --> 00:39:28,866
[♪ music fades]

630
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:30,493
You really are something else.

631
00:39:32,161 --> 00:39:34,497
As a teacher,
you killed two of your students.

632
00:39:35,874 --> 00:39:37,875
How can you live with that?

633
00:39:37,876 --> 00:39:41,545
[inhales sharply] What else could I
have done? There was no other way.

634
00:39:41,546 --> 00:39:42,672
[breath trembles]

635
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:46,383
They blackmailed me first,

636
00:39:46,384 --> 00:39:47,926
so this was self-defense.

637
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:50,929
If you had just admitted your crime,
no one would have died.

638
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:52,055
[scoffs]

639
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:53,348
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

640
00:39:53,349 --> 00:39:55,601
Who in the world would do that?

641
00:39:55,602 --> 00:39:57,895
[yelling] I have a name
and a reputation to uphold!

642
00:39:57,896 --> 00:40:00,314
You're the one
who tarnished that reputation.

643
00:40:00,315 --> 00:40:01,941
Now, people will remember you

644
00:40:03,026 --> 00:40:05,570
not as the legend of Korean dance,

645
00:40:06,988 --> 00:40:08,740
but as a murderer.

646
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:17,123
[sobbing softly]

647
00:40:22,503 --> 00:40:24,464
MOON SEYEON, MAY YOU REST IN PEACE

648
00:40:26,341 --> 00:40:28,091
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

649
00:40:28,092 --> 00:40:29,552
WE WILL MISS YOU, SEYEON

650
00:40:34,515 --> 00:40:35,808
[sniffling, sobbing]

651
00:40:39,729 --> 00:40:40,730
[sniffles]

652
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:48,613
My poor child. [sobbing bitterly]

653
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:57,163
My poor child.

654
00:40:58,998 --> 00:41:00,541
[♪ music increases in tempo]

655
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:06,839
PRINCIPAL JEONG JOOHEE

656
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:16,683
[shattering]

657
00:41:24,232 --> 00:41:25,233
[♪ music fades]

658
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,779
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

659
00:41:47,672 --> 00:41:48,797
[♪ music fades]

660
00:41:48,798 --> 00:41:49,881
CURSE CHARM

661
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:51,509
JUNYOUNG, KYUNGJIN
I CURSE YOU, BREAK UP

662
00:41:55,346 --> 00:41:56,430
Where's everyone?

663
00:41:56,431 --> 00:41:58,265
Off to meet their girlfriends. [sighs]

664
00:41:58,266 --> 00:42:00,642
Such romantics, aren't they?

665
00:42:00,643 --> 00:42:01,686
[chuckles softly]

666
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:04,855
Why don't us single folks
go get something to eat?

667
00:42:04,856 --> 00:42:07,357
Shall we go somewhere I know?
It's Michelin-starred.

668
00:42:07,358 --> 00:42:09,026
- Let's just go local. I'm hungry.
- [mouse clicking]

669
00:42:09,027 --> 00:42:11,611
You must have
a bottomless pit for a stomach.

670
00:42:11,612 --> 00:42:13,031
Wrap it up quickly.

671
00:42:14,032 --> 00:42:15,033
Oh, I'm starving.

672
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:17,952
I just need to finish this.

673
00:42:22,373 --> 00:42:23,875
[crunching]

674
00:42:29,630 --> 00:42:31,548
Mmm! It's delicious.

675
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:33,091
- It's good, right?
- Yeah.

676
00:42:33,092 --> 00:42:34,885
This is the best place around here.

677
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:37,888
Why go to a Michelin restaurant
when we have a place like this?

678
00:42:37,889 --> 00:42:40,224
Hey, Michelin is Michelin, so...

679
00:42:40,975 --> 00:42:44,061
[sighs in exasperation] Forget it.
Want a draft beer?

680
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:45,437
Yeah, sounds good.

681
00:42:45,438 --> 00:42:48,398
Can we have two...
No, one glass of draft beer, please.

682
00:42:48,399 --> 00:42:49,400
[server] Sure.

683
00:42:52,612 --> 00:42:53,820
Mmm!

684
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:54,822
That's good.

685
00:42:55,531 --> 00:42:58,910
By the way, that reed you gave me.

686
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:01,036
Yeah?

687
00:43:01,037 --> 00:43:03,997
Apparently, they can't determine
the exact location with that,

688
00:43:03,998 --> 00:43:06,041
because it's native to the west coast.

689
00:43:06,042 --> 00:43:07,627
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

690
00:43:08,461 --> 00:43:10,254
What are you going to do about Seongwon?

691
00:43:10,922 --> 00:43:12,298
I have someone watching him.

692
00:43:12,965 --> 00:43:14,884
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

693
00:43:23,267 --> 00:43:24,727
[Mr. Hwang] Welcome home, Young Master.

694
00:43:43,496 --> 00:43:44,497
[door closes]

695
00:43:46,666 --> 00:43:47,916
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

696
00:43:47,917 --> 00:43:49,043
[keyboard clacking]

697
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:58,803
Thank you.

698
00:43:59,679 --> 00:44:00,846
[cell phone vibrating]

699
00:44:00,847 --> 00:44:02,807
PI JEONG MINJAE

700
00:44:03,516 --> 00:44:04,599
Hello?

701
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,560
Yu Seongwon brought a woman to his studio.

702
00:44:06,561 --> 00:44:07,644
I'll head there first.

703
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:09,563
Okay, we're on our way.

704
00:44:09,564 --> 00:44:11,356
- [line disconnects]
- What's wrong?

705
00:44:11,357 --> 00:44:13,942
Yu Seongwon brought a woman to his studio.

706
00:44:13,943 --> 00:44:15,069
[♪ music swells]

707
00:44:17,113 --> 00:44:18,114
[♪ music fades]

708
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:25,204
[Areum] Your studio is really nice.

709
00:44:26,706 --> 00:44:29,584
[sighs] I wish I could work
in a studio like this.

710
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:34,255
You can work here anytime you want.

711
00:44:35,047 --> 00:44:37,133
- Really?
- Of course.

712
00:44:38,551 --> 00:44:39,886
[giggles excitedly]

713
00:44:43,306 --> 00:44:45,265
If you can make it here.

714
00:44:45,266 --> 00:44:46,934
[♪ ominous music playing]

715
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:58,195
- [camera shutter clicking]
- Why do you take photographs?

716
00:44:58,196 --> 00:45:00,823
To feel you while I work.

717
00:45:01,741 --> 00:45:03,701
Can I get a copy if they come out well?

718
00:45:04,952 --> 00:45:06,286
[chuckles softly]

719
00:45:06,287 --> 00:45:07,288
No.

720
00:45:10,333 --> 00:45:12,709
What kind of artwork
are you going to make me into?

721
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:14,753
I'm not sure. [sighs softly]

722
00:45:14,754 --> 00:45:16,464
I can't say I know you yet.

723
00:45:17,298 --> 00:45:18,965
What do you like most?

724
00:45:18,966 --> 00:45:21,343
I like painting the most.

725
00:45:21,344 --> 00:45:22,928
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

726
00:45:22,929 --> 00:45:24,347
I wish I could

727
00:45:25,181 --> 00:45:28,309
spend just one month painting,
without worrying about money.

728
00:45:28,935 --> 00:45:29,936
[scoffs]

729
00:45:30,937 --> 00:45:32,230
That's no fun.

730
00:45:33,022 --> 00:45:34,565
What's no fun?

731
00:45:36,359 --> 00:45:38,110
[♪ music increases in tempo]

732
00:45:54,252 --> 00:45:55,419
[liquid squirting]

733
00:46:01,300 --> 00:46:03,010
- [camera shutter clicks]
- Talk about something else.

734
00:46:03,761 --> 00:46:06,138
What was the worst thing you've ever done?

735
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:08,890
[chuckles softly] The worst thing?

736
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:09,892
[♪ music fades]

737
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:12,727
What about you?

738
00:46:12,728 --> 00:46:15,689
The worst thing I've done?

739
00:46:15,690 --> 00:46:17,525
[♪ ominous music playing]

740
00:46:20,486 --> 00:46:21,862
You'd be shocked if you knew.

741
00:46:23,281 --> 00:46:24,490
What was it?

742
00:46:29,328 --> 00:46:30,830
I gave my father

743
00:46:31,664 --> 00:46:33,124
a makeover.

744
00:46:37,712 --> 00:46:38,962
Your father?

745
00:46:38,963 --> 00:46:42,466
I put really heavy makeup on him.

746
00:46:45,678 --> 00:46:47,054
[♪ music swells]

747
00:46:49,390 --> 00:46:50,683
- [♪ music resumes tempo]
- Why?

748
00:46:52,685 --> 00:46:54,561
Because I didn't like his expression.

749
00:46:54,562 --> 00:46:55,730
[chuckles softly]

750
00:46:56,397 --> 00:46:58,149
Didn't he tell you off?

751
00:46:59,442 --> 00:47:00,818
He didn't say anything.

752
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:07,116
[exhales softly]

753
00:47:08,534 --> 00:47:09,952
Want a glass of champagne?

754
00:47:10,578 --> 00:47:12,037
[♪ ominous music continues]

755
00:47:12,038 --> 00:47:13,497
[footsteps approaching]

756
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:15,291
Any movements?

757
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:17,251
Not yet.

758
00:47:22,340 --> 00:47:23,631
Should we go in now?

759
00:47:23,632 --> 00:47:25,426
No, let's just wait.

760
00:47:26,052 --> 00:47:27,803
[♪ music increases in tempo]

761
00:47:40,649 --> 00:47:42,859
[♪ ominous sting]

762
00:47:42,860 --> 00:47:44,278
How do you want to die?

763
00:47:45,154 --> 00:47:46,237
What?

764
00:47:46,238 --> 00:47:48,573
How do you want to die?

765
00:47:48,574 --> 00:47:50,117
Have you never thought about that?

766
00:47:50,910 --> 00:47:52,077
[chuckles softly]

767
00:47:52,078 --> 00:47:53,495
[♪ ominous sting]

768
00:47:53,496 --> 00:47:54,789
Well,

769
00:47:56,332 --> 00:47:59,251
I'd want to die painlessly and peacefully.

770
00:47:59,835 --> 00:48:00,836
Peacefully?

771
00:48:01,420 --> 00:48:03,339
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

772
00:48:07,385 --> 00:48:08,677
That's nice, too.

773
00:48:14,767 --> 00:48:15,935
Drink up.

774
00:48:20,356 --> 00:48:22,358
[♪ ominous, ticking music playing]

775
00:48:26,946 --> 00:48:28,155
[♪ music swells]

776
00:48:31,325 --> 00:48:32,575
[car horn blaring]

777
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:34,369
- [♪ music fades]
- [car horn honking]

778
00:48:34,370 --> 00:48:36,496
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

779
00:48:36,497 --> 00:48:37,873
[car horn honking]

780
00:48:39,542 --> 00:48:41,752
[car horn honking, blaring]

781
00:48:49,176 --> 00:48:51,262
Young Master Isoo is here.

782
00:48:55,057 --> 00:48:56,225
[sighs deeply]

783
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:58,060
[chuckles]

784
00:48:59,562 --> 00:49:01,063
We have an unwanted guest.

785
00:49:07,653 --> 00:49:09,946
Sorry to drop in so late. Can I come in?

786
00:49:09,947 --> 00:49:12,450
- Oh. Yes, of course.
- Thanks.

787
00:49:20,291 --> 00:49:22,626
[♪ music swells, fades]

788
00:49:27,047 --> 00:49:28,131
Isoo!

789
00:49:28,132 --> 00:49:30,133
What brings you here out of the blue?

790
00:49:30,134 --> 00:49:32,219
I just remembered you said you liked this.

791
00:49:32,928 --> 00:49:35,430
Here. We'll drink one bottle now.

792
00:49:35,431 --> 00:49:36,640
Thank you.

793
00:49:38,767 --> 00:49:40,019
You have a guest.

794
00:49:40,895 --> 00:49:42,979
Ah, you must be his model.

795
00:49:42,980 --> 00:49:46,442
[chuckles softly]
Yes. Aren't you Jin Isoo?

796
00:49:47,193 --> 00:49:49,611
She knows me. She must be a fan.

797
00:49:49,612 --> 00:49:51,154
Would you like a photo?

798
00:49:51,155 --> 00:49:52,448
- Really?
- Yes.

799
00:49:54,450 --> 00:49:55,534
All right.

800
00:49:56,285 --> 00:49:57,995
- One, two, three.
- [camera shutter clicks]

801
00:49:58,662 --> 00:50:00,914
Nice to meet you. What's your name?

802
00:50:00,915 --> 00:50:02,207
Song Areum.

803
00:50:02,208 --> 00:50:03,791
Areum.

804
00:50:03,792 --> 00:50:06,169
Would you like to join us for a drink?
I made this.

805
00:50:06,170 --> 00:50:07,171
No.

806
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:08,714
Uh...

807
00:50:09,215 --> 00:50:11,342
Areum should probably get going.

808
00:50:12,218 --> 00:50:13,593
Let's do this another time.

809
00:50:13,594 --> 00:50:14,677
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

810
00:50:14,678 --> 00:50:15,763
[Areum] Ah.

811
00:50:16,138 --> 00:50:17,347
[chuckles softly]

812
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:18,349
Okay, sure.

813
00:50:18,933 --> 00:50:21,434
Mmm, then I'll have to call you a cab.

814
00:50:21,435 --> 00:50:24,855
The premium kind. One second. Ah...

815
00:50:26,815 --> 00:50:28,233
Your cab's here.

816
00:50:28,234 --> 00:50:29,400
Wear your seatbelt.

817
00:50:29,401 --> 00:50:30,568
- Okay.
- Right.

818
00:50:30,569 --> 00:50:31,862
[exhales contentedly]

819
00:50:33,906 --> 00:50:35,533
You look like a skilled driver.

820
00:50:36,242 --> 00:50:38,536
Please take her home safely. Bye.

821
00:50:48,128 --> 00:50:50,089
Seriously, what the heck?

822
00:50:51,173 --> 00:50:53,800
What do you mean?
Come on, let's go have a drink.

823
00:50:53,801 --> 00:50:54,926
Let's go.

824
00:50:54,927 --> 00:50:56,302
[♪ music increases in tempo]

825
00:50:56,303 --> 00:50:57,429
Let's go!

826
00:51:07,606 --> 00:51:09,233
- [♪ music resumes tempo]
- [Hyera panting] Wait.

827
00:51:11,360 --> 00:51:12,569
I'm a detective.

828
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:13,654
[♪ music fades]

829
00:51:15,072 --> 00:51:16,740
You were with Yu Seongwon, weren't you?

830
00:51:19,618 --> 00:51:20,619
Yes.

831
00:51:21,161 --> 00:51:22,371
What's going on?

832
00:51:22,913 --> 00:51:24,998
Could I talk to you for a second?

833
00:51:24,999 --> 00:51:27,333
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

834
00:51:27,334 --> 00:51:31,129
I work part-time as a bartender.
I met him at the bar.

835
00:51:31,130 --> 00:51:32,964
Did he ask you to be his model?

836
00:51:32,965 --> 00:51:34,091
Yes.

837
00:51:35,301 --> 00:51:37,386
But what's this all about?

838
00:51:37,970 --> 00:51:41,640
Two of Yu Seongwon's models are missing.

839
00:51:42,308 --> 00:51:44,101
What do you mean?

840
00:51:45,060 --> 00:51:46,686
We're investigating those cases.

841
00:51:46,687 --> 00:51:49,063
[♪ pulsating, suspenseful music playing]

842
00:51:49,064 --> 00:51:50,398
No wonder.

843
00:51:50,399 --> 00:51:53,943
He said something
that was kind of disturbing.

844
00:51:53,944 --> 00:51:55,195
Like what?

845
00:51:56,739 --> 00:51:58,615
How do you want to die?

846
00:51:58,616 --> 00:51:59,742
[Hyera exhales softly]

847
00:52:03,245 --> 00:52:05,873
You shouldn't meet him
even if he calls you again.

848
00:52:06,373 --> 00:52:07,457
Okay.

849
00:52:07,458 --> 00:52:08,875
If he contacts you,

850
00:52:08,876 --> 00:52:10,919
please let me know.

851
00:52:14,131 --> 00:52:15,257
[♪ music fades]

852
00:52:15,841 --> 00:52:17,009
[Isoo] Hey, are you mad at me?

853
00:52:17,676 --> 00:52:19,636
Who's more important to you,
me or the model?

854
00:52:19,637 --> 00:52:23,264
It's been a while
since I found a model I liked, Isoo.

855
00:52:23,265 --> 00:52:25,183
[sighs] Drink up.

856
00:52:25,184 --> 00:52:26,602
Get inspiration from me today.

857
00:52:28,103 --> 00:52:29,104
[clink]

858
00:52:32,483 --> 00:52:34,651
- Hey, Seongwon.
- Yeah?

859
00:52:34,652 --> 00:52:38,071
You said you met me when you were little.

860
00:52:38,072 --> 00:52:39,907
- Yeah.
- When was that?

861
00:52:40,866 --> 00:52:42,660
[sighs deeply] Seriously.

862
00:52:43,661 --> 00:52:46,329
It annoys me that you don't remember,
so I'm not telling you.

863
00:52:46,330 --> 00:52:48,749
At least give me a hint.

864
00:52:53,170 --> 00:52:54,713
Back then,

865
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:57,299
you were a lot quieter than you are now.

866
00:52:59,385 --> 00:53:02,387
You were shorter and thinner.

867
00:53:02,388 --> 00:53:03,639
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

868
00:53:04,306 --> 00:53:05,974
The hallway was bright,

869
00:53:07,685 --> 00:53:10,270
and a breeze was coming in
through the window.

870
00:53:12,940 --> 00:53:14,148
SEO YUKYUNG PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

871
00:53:14,149 --> 00:53:15,651
<i>It was quiet</i>

872
00:53:16,443 --> 00:53:17,861
<i>and dull.</i>

873
00:53:20,030 --> 00:53:24,368
<i>Surrounded by white walls,
it was the same thing day after day,</i>

874
00:53:29,039 --> 00:53:32,542
<i>but then, you suddenly sat next to me.</i>

875
00:53:32,543 --> 00:53:35,254
Hey, what's your name?

876
00:53:38,716 --> 00:53:39,967
What are you sick with?

877
00:53:45,305 --> 00:53:46,390
How's my drawing?

878
00:53:49,935 --> 00:53:51,269
It's really good.

879
00:53:51,270 --> 00:53:53,063
Do you know what this is?

880
00:53:53,772 --> 00:53:54,815
It's a puppy.

881
00:54:03,782 --> 00:54:05,700
[door opens]

882
00:54:05,701 --> 00:54:07,201
[Dr. Seo] Jin Isoo.

883
00:54:07,202 --> 00:54:08,495
Come inside.

884
00:54:19,715 --> 00:54:20,841
Jin Isoo.

885
00:54:25,763 --> 00:54:26,764
[chuckles softly]

886
00:54:28,557 --> 00:54:29,558
My picture.

887
00:54:30,392 --> 00:54:32,894
Everyone said it was weird.

888
00:54:32,895 --> 00:54:35,189
You were the only person
who complimented me.

889
00:54:42,279 --> 00:54:43,405
Do you know why?

890
00:54:44,656 --> 00:54:47,451
You recognized it
because you and I are alike.

891
00:54:49,286 --> 00:54:52,121
In what way are we alike?

892
00:54:52,122 --> 00:54:53,207
[exhales softly]

893
00:54:54,875 --> 00:54:56,043
Your mom.

894
00:54:58,545 --> 00:55:01,590
You said you were with her when she died.

895
00:55:02,174 --> 00:55:03,175
[Seongwon] Huh?

896
00:55:05,177 --> 00:55:06,470
How did it feel?

897
00:55:09,306 --> 00:55:11,642
Did you witness the moment she died?

898
00:55:12,434 --> 00:55:14,436
When her soul left her eyes?

899
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:16,687
That very moment?

900
00:55:16,688 --> 00:55:17,898
[♪ music swells]

901
00:55:20,651 --> 00:55:21,902
[♪ music fades]

902
00:55:24,279 --> 00:55:25,322
[door opens]

903
00:55:26,323 --> 00:55:27,324
[door closes]

904
00:55:30,661 --> 00:55:32,245
This is Detective Jin Isoo.

905
00:55:32,246 --> 00:55:33,913
This is private investigator Jeong Minjae.

906
00:55:33,914 --> 00:55:35,874
He used to work at Violent Crime with me.

907
00:55:36,500 --> 00:55:37,834
Oh, it's nice to meet you.

908
00:55:38,460 --> 00:55:40,127
You really helped us out today.

909
00:55:40,128 --> 00:55:41,380
Not at all.

910
00:55:42,256 --> 00:55:43,757
So, what did Areum say?

911
00:55:44,341 --> 00:55:46,759
They met by chance,
and he asked her to be his model.

912
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:47,761
[Isoo] Hmm.

913
00:55:48,512 --> 00:55:50,304
Did you talk to him?

914
00:55:50,305 --> 00:55:53,266
He said I met him when I was young,

915
00:55:53,267 --> 00:55:56,144
but I honestly don't remember.

916
00:55:59,856 --> 00:56:01,108
What are you going to do now?

917
00:56:01,817 --> 00:56:03,277
We'll have to keep watching.

918
00:56:04,027 --> 00:56:06,321
He might go on a rampage
now that we've stopped him.

919
00:56:06,905 --> 00:56:07,906
[Isoo sighs softly]

920
00:56:16,915 --> 00:56:18,124
[sighs softly]

921
00:56:18,125 --> 00:56:19,585
[footsteps approaching]

922
00:56:28,135 --> 00:56:30,053
[crockery clinking]

923
00:56:31,471 --> 00:56:32,639
[sighs wearily]

924
00:56:36,101 --> 00:56:38,102
I bring Areum home...

925
00:56:38,103 --> 00:56:39,855
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

926
00:56:43,525 --> 00:56:47,112
<i>- ...and he barges in an hour later?
-</i> [car horn honking, blaring]

927
00:56:47,988 --> 00:56:48,989
[scoffs softly]

928
00:56:50,616 --> 00:56:51,742
That's strange.

929
00:56:52,618 --> 00:56:53,619
Right?

930
00:56:57,873 --> 00:56:59,374
[sighs deeply]

931
00:57:00,667 --> 00:57:01,960
[♪ music fades]

932
00:57:03,962 --> 00:57:04,963
[slurps]

933
00:57:05,797 --> 00:57:06,923
[exhales deeply]

934
00:57:08,634 --> 00:57:10,552
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

935
00:57:13,180 --> 00:57:14,181
What the heck?

936
00:57:23,815 --> 00:57:24,940
[sighs wearily]

937
00:57:24,941 --> 00:57:26,234
[♪ music swells]

938
00:57:30,530 --> 00:57:31,657
[sighs softly]

939
00:57:34,951 --> 00:57:36,035
[♪ music fades]

940
00:57:36,036 --> 00:57:37,079
Did Isoo...

941
00:57:38,914 --> 00:57:41,123
side with Joo Hyera?

942
00:57:41,124 --> 00:57:42,250
[♪ suspenseful sting]

943
00:57:46,380 --> 00:57:47,797
[cell phone ringing over car audio]

944
00:57:47,798 --> 00:57:49,383
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA
INCOMING CALL

945
00:57:50,884 --> 00:57:53,094
[Hyera] <i>Yu Seongwon found our cameras.</i>

946
00:57:53,095 --> 00:57:54,887
<i>He destroyed them all.</i>

947
00:57:54,888 --> 00:57:56,347
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

948
00:57:56,348 --> 00:57:57,766
We have no way of watching him.

949
00:58:00,477 --> 00:58:01,687
I'll look into it.

950
00:58:07,025 --> 00:58:08,150
MR. CHOI

951
00:58:08,151 --> 00:58:09,778
[line connects, ringing]

952
00:58:11,279 --> 00:58:13,572
[Isoo] Mr. Choi, I have a favor to ask.

953
00:58:13,573 --> 00:58:14,866
[engine revving]

954
00:58:19,121 --> 00:58:20,204
HANSU AIR SPACE

955
00:58:20,205 --> 00:58:21,456
[tires screeching]

956
00:58:23,917 --> 00:58:25,084
[♪ music fades]

957
00:58:25,085 --> 00:58:27,878
Ah, why did you come? I can go by myself.

958
00:58:27,879 --> 00:58:30,047
I thought I might as well come see you.

959
00:58:30,048 --> 00:58:31,507
How are you feeling?

960
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:33,092
- [inhales sharply]
- [exhales sharply]

961
00:58:33,093 --> 00:58:34,468
It's a secret.

962
00:58:34,469 --> 00:58:35,553
[whispering] How are you?

963
00:58:35,554 --> 00:58:38,431
I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

964
00:58:38,432 --> 00:58:39,932
What did the hospital say?

965
00:58:39,933 --> 00:58:42,309
They're going to monitor me for a while,

966
00:58:42,310 --> 00:58:44,478
but I'm doing well so far.

967
00:58:44,479 --> 00:58:45,981
[sighs in relief] That's such a relief.

968
00:58:47,107 --> 00:58:48,858
What about you?

969
00:58:48,859 --> 00:58:51,694
I'm taking medication and doing okay.

970
00:58:51,695 --> 00:58:52,778
Really?

971
00:58:52,779 --> 00:58:55,740
Really. You should
worry about yourself first.

972
00:58:55,741 --> 00:58:56,992
[clicks tongue] Don't get sick.

973
00:58:58,243 --> 00:58:59,703
- Right.
- Let's go.

974
00:59:00,954 --> 00:59:02,581
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

975
00:59:09,921 --> 00:59:11,423
Thank you all for your hard work.

976
00:59:12,215 --> 00:59:14,134
Don't mind us. Please carry on.

977
00:59:16,678 --> 00:59:18,472
It's been a while, Chief.

978
00:59:20,223 --> 00:59:21,308
[♪ music fades]

979
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:25,853
Yes, please move it

980
00:59:25,854 --> 00:59:27,605
right here.

981
00:59:27,606 --> 00:59:29,565
[♪ quirky music playing]

982
00:59:29,566 --> 00:59:31,734
What is it for?

983
00:59:31,735 --> 00:59:35,029
Uh, you'll be in danger if you know.

984
00:59:35,030 --> 00:59:37,032
Please set it up
so I can watch the live feed.

985
00:59:38,992 --> 00:59:40,410
Please do as he says.

986
00:59:42,829 --> 00:59:44,622
- [♪ music fades]
- So what exactly is this again?

987
00:59:44,623 --> 00:59:47,458
- Mmm, a high-altitude UAV.
- [keyboard clacking]

988
00:59:47,459 --> 00:59:49,503
A drone that can fly for a long time.

989
00:59:51,463 --> 00:59:53,089
And it belongs to Hansu Group?

990
00:59:54,007 --> 00:59:56,425
Yes. Some are supplied to the military,

991
00:59:56,426 --> 00:59:58,093
others are used to monitor wildfires,

992
00:59:58,094 --> 01:00:00,346
and one was in the air just for testing,

993
01:00:00,347 --> 01:00:02,265
so I moved that one to Seongwon's studio.

994
01:00:03,225 --> 01:00:04,226
Oh!

995
01:00:06,645 --> 01:00:08,313
[Isoo] Four, three,

996
01:00:09,064 --> 01:00:10,106
five, three, zero.

997
01:00:11,441 --> 01:00:12,901
- [in English] Connect.
- [digital beeping]

998
01:00:16,696 --> 01:00:18,239
[in Korean] It's live.

999
01:00:18,240 --> 01:00:19,490
This should do, right?

1000
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:21,117
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

1001
01:00:22,327 --> 01:00:23,410
Whoa.

1002
01:00:23,411 --> 01:00:25,746
I've never seen
such a cool chaebol before.

1003
01:00:25,747 --> 01:00:27,081
You're so cool, Detective Jin.

1004
01:00:27,082 --> 01:00:29,041
You've never seen a chaebol before?

1005
01:00:29,042 --> 01:00:30,125
It's no big deal.

1006
01:00:30,126 --> 01:00:32,586
Uh-uh. No, Jin Isoo.

1007
01:00:32,587 --> 01:00:34,129
You're impressive.

1008
01:00:34,130 --> 01:00:35,339
[all chuckling]

1009
01:00:35,340 --> 01:00:37,341
Really? This is nothing.

1010
01:00:37,342 --> 01:00:38,510
Honestly.

1011
01:00:40,595 --> 01:00:41,721
- [Minjae sighs]
- [♪ music fades]

1012
01:00:42,639 --> 01:00:44,974
If I was going to work
with someone like you,

1013
01:00:44,975 --> 01:00:46,852
I seriously wouldn't have quit.

1014
01:00:47,477 --> 01:00:50,229
How can you say that
when you quit after working with me?

1015
01:00:50,230 --> 01:00:52,523
Well, it's true.

1016
01:00:52,524 --> 01:00:53,775
Is there anything you can't do?

1017
01:00:54,526 --> 01:00:56,986
Not much, really. Mmm.

1018
01:00:56,987 --> 01:00:58,153
[chuckles]

1019
01:00:58,154 --> 01:01:02,241
This is a guy who buys an entire house
just because he wants to see the basement.

1020
01:01:02,242 --> 01:01:03,701
[♪ soft piano music playing in background]

1021
01:01:03,702 --> 01:01:05,328
[exhales incredulously] That's crazy.

1022
01:01:05,996 --> 01:01:09,248
Hyera, doesn't that give you
a huge dopamine rush?

1023
01:01:09,249 --> 01:01:12,668
- Is your brain okay?
- Every day is a roller coaster. Mmm.

1024
01:01:12,669 --> 01:01:14,503
The car we were driving blows up,

1025
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:16,505
twin magicians show up.

1026
01:01:16,506 --> 01:01:19,301
That sounds so much fun. I'm jealous.

1027
01:01:20,135 --> 01:01:22,220
Join us. Come work for me.

1028
01:01:23,763 --> 01:01:25,264
Should I try joining the force again?

1029
01:01:25,265 --> 01:01:26,349
[chuckles]

1030
01:01:28,226 --> 01:01:30,562
- Hey, where are you going?
- The restroom.

1031
01:01:35,108 --> 01:01:36,525
[door opens]

1032
01:01:36,526 --> 01:01:37,944
- [sighs deeply]
- [door closes]

1033
01:01:39,446 --> 01:01:40,447
[Minjae] Thank you.

1034
01:01:41,740 --> 01:01:43,450
Kim Heejun's death

1035
01:01:44,284 --> 01:01:45,869
was a weight on her conscience.

1036
01:01:46,995 --> 01:01:48,078
And for me, too.

1037
01:01:48,079 --> 01:01:49,915
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

1038
01:01:50,957 --> 01:01:53,376
Couldn't we have prevented it?

1039
01:01:54,836 --> 01:01:56,504
Was it maybe our fault?

1040
01:01:59,633 --> 01:02:01,468
I ran away from that like a coward,

1041
01:02:03,136 --> 01:02:04,596
while Hyera just endured it.

1042
01:02:06,723 --> 01:02:09,267
Saving Areum means a lot to us.

1043
01:02:13,980 --> 01:02:18,151
If it's with you, I think
we'll be able to catch Yu Seongwon.

1044
01:02:19,361 --> 01:02:20,737
Of course, we can, huh.

1045
01:02:21,237 --> 01:02:22,739
We'll catch that bastard

1046
01:02:23,365 --> 01:02:26,158
and isolate him from society for good.

1047
01:02:26,159 --> 01:02:27,534
- Cheers.
- [Minjae] Cheers.

1048
01:02:27,535 --> 01:02:28,828
- [Hyera] Hey, me too.
- [door closes]

1049
01:02:29,955 --> 01:02:30,997
[chuckles softly]

1050
01:02:31,665 --> 01:02:33,749
All right, let's do this.

1051
01:02:33,750 --> 01:02:34,960
- Let's do this!
- Let's do this!

1052
01:02:38,672 --> 01:02:39,714
[♪ music fades]

1053
01:02:49,557 --> 01:02:50,683
[groans]

1054
01:02:50,684 --> 01:02:52,435
God, my head. [sighs]

1055
01:02:56,272 --> 01:02:58,858
[sighs] I must be out of my mind.

1056
01:03:00,902 --> 01:03:01,987
[sighs wearily]

1057
01:03:03,488 --> 01:03:05,615
[chuckles] Roller coaster.

1058
01:03:08,243 --> 01:03:10,370
[grunts, groans]

1059
01:03:12,163 --> 01:03:14,040
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1060
01:03:17,585 --> 01:03:18,962
[♪ music swells]

1061
01:03:22,257 --> 01:03:23,382
What's all this?

1062
01:03:23,383 --> 01:03:24,968
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

1063
01:03:44,654 --> 01:03:46,072
[♪ music turns ominous]

1064
01:03:50,493 --> 01:03:52,245
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1065
01:03:55,331 --> 01:03:56,707
[Younghwan laughing] Huh?

1066
01:03:56,708 --> 01:03:58,334
<i>My friend, Jin Isoo.</i> [laughs]

1067
01:04:00,462 --> 01:04:01,504
[Isoo] <i>Younghwan, you, again!</i>

1068
01:04:02,213 --> 01:04:03,297
You want to try, too?

1069
01:04:03,298 --> 01:04:05,299
No! Please... Don't!

1070
01:04:05,300 --> 01:04:08,261
I told you I'd never see you
if you did it again.

1071
01:04:14,684 --> 01:04:17,102
<i>You should undergo
a proper investigation and quit drugs.</i>

1072
01:04:17,103 --> 01:04:20,482
All my life,
I've never thought of you as a friend.

1073
01:04:22,942 --> 01:04:24,527
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1074
01:04:28,239 --> 01:04:29,282
Jin Isoo.

1075
01:04:32,869 --> 01:04:34,079
[♪ music swells]

1076
01:04:47,300 --> 01:04:48,383
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 10

1077
01:04:48,384 --> 01:04:49,885
A BLOOD TRAIL SURROUNDS JIN ISOO

1078
01:04:49,886 --> 01:04:52,055
[♪ mellow emotional music playing]

1079
01:05:14,410 --> 01:05:17,831
Special Cast. Jeon Hyebin

1080
01:05:25,797 --> 01:05:26,880
What happened?

1081
01:05:26,881 --> 01:05:28,465
[Junyoung] He's Isoo's
middle school classmate.

1082
01:05:28,466 --> 01:05:30,259
Get a grip.
You have to remember something!

1083
01:05:30,260 --> 01:05:33,220
[detective] <i>Jin Isoo, you're under arrest
for the murder of Kim Younghwan.</i>

1084
01:05:33,221 --> 01:05:34,763
- You two fought, didn't you?
- Yes.

1085
01:05:34,764 --> 01:05:36,265
[Younghwan] <i>Your friend
came to see you, punk.</i>

1086
01:05:36,266 --> 01:05:37,349
You're finished.

1087
01:05:37,350 --> 01:05:38,642
I heard someone reported me.

1088
01:05:38,643 --> 01:05:40,394
[Isoo, over recording] <i>I killed someone.</i>

1089
01:05:40,395 --> 01:05:41,520
Got nothing left to deny?

1090
01:05:41,521 --> 01:05:43,063
[Hyera] <i>They went in with a set narrative.</i>

1091
01:05:43,064 --> 01:05:44,690
We're from Internal Affairs.

1092
01:05:44,691 --> 01:05:46,567
They found a high dose
of drugs in his system.

1093
01:05:46,568 --> 01:05:49,153
Does taking that drug
for the first time make you violent?

1094
01:05:49,154 --> 01:05:51,488
People with a lot
of pent-up anger tend to snap.

1095
01:05:51,489 --> 01:05:52,906
[Seongwon] <i>Jin Isoo could be the killer.</i>

1096
01:05:52,907 --> 01:05:55,492
Isoo! Maybe you've been holding it all in.

1097
01:05:55,493 --> 01:05:57,453
<i>And it just blew up on Younghwan.</i>

1098
01:05:58,413 --> 01:06:00,205
- [bang]
- Once you admit it,

1099
01:06:00,206 --> 01:06:01,790
you will be free.

1100
01:06:01,791 --> 01:06:02,876
[♪ song fades]

1101
01:06:04,752 --> 01:06:06,421
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1102
01:06:13,928 --> 01:06:15,220
[Younghwan] <i>Jin Isoo.</i>

1103
01:06:15,221 --> 01:06:16,347
<i>Goodbye.</i>

1104
01:06:18,683 --> 01:06:20,518
[Younghwan laughing maniacally]

1105
01:06:37,577 --> 01:06:38,744
[squelch]

1106
01:06:38,745 --> 01:06:39,913
[♪ music swells]

1107
01:06:44,584 --> 01:06:45,918
[♪ music fades]

1108
01:06:45,919 --> 01:06:47,921
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
